scenario: reset-fails
Z         commit(), then close()                                                                       returned normally
A         getSchema() (pgjdbc runs select current_schema())                                            public
observer  pool backend before A's close()                                                              state=idle in transaction xact_open=true xid=false xmin=true
observer  committed probe_row.v = 1 after A's last statement                                           done
A         close()                                                                                      threw SQLException SQLSTATE 25001: Cannot change transaction isolation level in the middle of a transaction.
observer  pool backend after A's close()                                                               no backend
B         same physical session as A                                                                   false
B         getTransactionIsolation() through the pool                                                   READ_COMMITTED
B         show transaction_isolation                                                                   read committed
B         B's first statement is not its transaction's first (now() < statement_timestamp() - 500 ms)  false
B         probe_row.v as B reads it (observer committed 1)                                             1
observer  where B's committed insert landed                                                            public/ssc_app
B         close()                                                                                      returned normally
C         same physical session as A                                                                   false
C         show transaction_isolation                                                                   read committed
C         close()                                                                                      returned normally
